"binary-numbers:floating-point-rounding":{"type":"foundation","label":{"zh":"有限的位只能表示有限个数","en":"Finite bits hold finitely many numbers"},"reason":{"zh":"第 10 章从第 3 章的位权出发：0.1 在二进制里是无限循环小数，存进 52 位尾数就要就近取整，0.1 + 0.2 比 0.3 的最近值大一格。","en":"Chapter 10 starts from chapter 3’s place values: 0.1 is a repeating fraction in binary, so storing it in a 52-bit significand rounds it, and 0.1 + 0.2 lands one step above the nearest value to 0.3."},"source":"../computing/systems/switches-that-compute/#ch10"},
"binary-numbers:ripple-carry-adder":{"type":"foundation","label":{"zh":"每一列做同一件事","en":"Every column does the same thing"},"reason":{"zh":"第 4 章在第 3 章的二进制位上逐列相加：两位加进位，交出和位与进位；8 位加法器用 120 个与非门。","en":"Chapter 4 adds chapter 3’s binary digits column by column: two bits plus a carry give a sum bit and a carry; the 8-bit adder uses 120 NAND gates."},"source":"../computing/systems/switches-that-compute/#ch4"},
"binary-search:binary-numbers":{"type":"connection","label":{"zh":"n 次二分对应 n 位","en":"n halvings, n bits"},"reason":{"zh":"第 3 章把二分查找列为相关页：n 个开关有 2ⁿ 种样子，正如 n 次二分能在 2ⁿ 个候选里找到一个。","en":"Chapter 3 lists Binary Search as related: n switches have 2ⁿ patterns, just as n halvings find one of 2ⁿ candidates."},"source":"../computing/systems/switches-that-compute/#ch3"},
"binary-search:exp-log":{"type":"foundation","label":{"zh":"砍半次数就是对数","en":"The halving count is the logarithm"},"reason":{"zh":"二分查找每步砍掉一半，n 个数约 log₂n 步：对数数的正是“砍几次到 1”；反过来，汉诺塔的指数增长就是对数的逆过程。","en":"Binary search halves each step, taking about log₂n steps for n items: the logarithm counts exactly \"how many halvings to 1\"; reversed, the Tower of Hanoi's exponential growth is the logarithm's inverse."},"source":"../computing/algorithms/recursion-divide/#step3"},
"block-file-object-storage:iscsi":{"type":"foundation","label":{"zh":"块级的那一行","en":"The block-level row"},"reason":{"zh":"第 3 章展开第 1 章表里块级的 iSCSI：要的是编了号的块，文件系统留在客户端。","en":"Chapter 3 expands the block-level iSCSI row of chapter 1's table: the client asks for numbered blocks and keeps the file system itself."},"source":"../computing/systems/storage-over-a-network/#ch3"},
