"bus-loading-reflected-wave:pcie-topology":{"type":"connection","label":{"zh":"每个设备一条串行链路","en":"One serial link per device"},"reason":{"zh":"第 2 章的结尾说：一段总线只剩一个插槽时，不如每个设备一条串行点对点链路，这就是《PCIe 为什么能一代一代翻倍》第 1 章的树。","en":"Chapter 2 ends: once a bus segment holds one slot, give each device its own serial point-to-point link; that is the tree of chapter 1 of “Why PCIe Keeps Doubling”."},"source":"../computing/systems/how-a-computer-is-wired/#ch2"},
"cache-address-split:cache-associativity-3c":{"type":"foundation","label":{"zh":"组号选出一组，再在组里比标记","en":"The index picks a set; the tag is compared within it"},"reason":{"zh":"第 3 章的组相联缓存沿用第 2 章把地址拆成标记、组号、偏移的办法，只是每组放进几路。","en":"Chapter 3’s set-associative cache keeps chapter 2’s split of an address into tag, index and offset, with several ways per set."},"source":"../computing/systems/how-cpu-caches-work/#ch3"},
"cache-address-split:false-sharing":{"type":"foundation","label":{"zh":"一致性按整行算","en":"Coherence works on whole lines"},"reason":{"zh":"第 9 章的伪共享发生，是因为第 2 章的 64 字节缓存行是缓存搬运和记账的最小单位，两个变量同在一行就会互相作废。","en":"Chapter 9’s false sharing happens because chapter 2’s 64-byte line is the unit caches move and track, so two variables in one line invalidate each other."},"source":"../computing/systems/how-cpu-caches-work/#ch9"},
