"thunderbolt-usb4-pcie-tunnel:usb4-bandwidth-allocation":{"type":"foundation","label":{"zh":"一块盘之后，几样东西挤在一起","en":"From one drive to a crowded link"},"reason":{"zh":"第 3 章从《移动硬盘为什么跑不满》第 8 章一块盘单独走 PCIe 隧道出发，看它和显示器、USB 设备挤在一起时分到多少。","en":"Chapter 3 starts from one drive alone on the PCIe tunnel in chapter 8 of “Why a USB Drive Never Hits Its Label” and asks what it gets when a display and USB device share the link."},"source":"../computing/systems/how-thunderbolt-works/#ch3"},
"thunderbolt-vs-usb4-requirements:thunderbolt-usb4-pcie-tunnel":{"type":"connection","label":{"zh":"PCIe 隧道是必选还是可选","en":"Is the PCIe tunnel required"},"reason":{"zh":"《移动硬盘为什么跑不满》第 8 章说 USB4 主机的 PCIe 隧道是可选的；第 9 章列出雷电 4、5 把哪些「可以」变成「必须」。","en":"Chapter 8 of “Why a USB Drive Never Hits Its Label” says PCIe tunnelling is optional on a USB4 host; chapter 9 lists what Thunderbolt 4 and 5 turn from optional into required."},"source":"../computing/systems/how-usb-drives-talk/#ch8"},
"tlb-and-reach:context-switch-tlb":{"type":"foundation","label":{"zh":"换进程时 TLB 怎么办","en":"What the TLB does on a switch"},"reason":{"zh":"第 10 章讲第 4 章的 TLB 在进程切换、进出内核时要不要清空，PCID 和 KPTI 都是这个问题。","en":"Chapter 10 asks whether chapter 4’s TLB must be flushed on a process switch or a kernel entry; PCID and KPTI are both that question."},"source":"../computing/systems/how-virtual-memory-works/#ch10"},
